codex
The rework’s architecture is materially different from the rejected version: recorders now do zero-timeout admission into a fixed 256-update serial lane, and snapshot construction runs behind that lane while producers can return or count saturation. The finite domain-bound error catalog, sequence-zero/reset/exhaustion path, and populated nested allowlists are present. I’m moving to independent execution checks now.
